{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_iff_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_iff_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L275-L282","doc":"The two directions together: neutrality is *exactly* meson-and-baryon\ncontent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.adjoint_triality_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.adjoint_triality_zero","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L271-L273","doc":"The adjoint, by contrast, *is* self-dual — triality `0`.  Recorded so the\ncertificate is seen to discriminate rather than to fire on everything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.fundamental_not_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.fundamental_not_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L260-L269","doc":"**The fundamental `𝟑` is complex type.**  Its triality is `1 ≠ 0`, so it is\nnot isomorphic to its dual.\n\nThis is the fact `Sym2GateFSTrichotomy` leaves as an input, obtained here from\nthe grading rather than cited.  What remains cited for the octonionic route is\nthe *other* half: that the Günaydin–Gürsey decomposition `Im(𝕆) ≅ ℝ ⊕ ℂ³` puts\n`SU(3)` on that `ℂ³` in its standard fundamental representation.  Given that,\ncomplex type is no longer an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.not_selfDual_of_triality_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.not_selfDual_of_triality_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L254-L258","doc":"**The certificate.**  An object of non-vanishing triality is *not*\nself-dual — so it is complex type, not real and not quaternionic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality_eq_zero_of_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality_eq_zero_of_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L243-L252","doc":"**Self-duality forces vanishing triality.**  In `ℤ/3`, `−x = x` gives\n`2x = 0`, and `2` is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality_dual","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L238-L241","doc":"Duality exchanges fundamentals and antifundamentals, hence negates\ntriality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.identification_agrees_on_hadrons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.identification_agrees_on_hadrons","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L216-L225","doc":"Concretely, on the whole hadron table at once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.identification_invisible_to_selection_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.identification_invisible_to_selection_rule","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L207-L214","doc":"**The proved negative.**  Identifying colour with flavour doubles each\nquark's triality, and that is invisible to the selection rule — every composite\nreceives the same verdict.  So triality cannot discriminate between the two\ncases, and the open question `flavour vs colour SU(3)` is not settled, or even\nnarrowed, by this grading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.trialityWeighted_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.trialityWeighted_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L199-L205","doc":"Weighting by a unit changes nothing: `ℤ/3` is a field, so `k·x = 0` forces\n`x = 0` whenever `k ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.trialityWeighted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.trialityWeighted","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L190-L197","doc":"**Weighted triality.**  If each quark carries `k` fundamental indices of the\ngroup, its triality is `k` and a composite of `a` quarks and `b` antiquarks has\ngrading `k·(a − b)`.\n\n`k = 1` is the case where colour and flavour are **distinct** groups (one colour\nindex per quark); `k = 2` is the case where they are **identified** (the colour\nand flavour indices become two indices of the same group). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L175-L186","doc":"**The converse, and the point of the file.**  Every colour-neutral\ncombination *is* `m` mesons together with `n` baryons and `n'` antibaryons.\n\nSo mesons and baryons are not merely examples of neutral states — the neutral\nmonoid is generated by `(1,1)`, `(3,0)` and `(0,3)`, and there is no third kind\nof colour-neutral composite to look for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.decomposition_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.decomposition_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L170-L173","doc":"Anything built from `m` mesons, `n` baryons and `n'` antibaryons is\nneutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.pentaquark_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.pentaquark_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L165-L166","doc":"The observed pentaquark `qqqq q̄` is neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.tetraquark_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.tetraquark_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L162-L163","doc":"The observed tetraquark `qq q̄q̄` is neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.four_quark_not_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.four_quark_not_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L159-L160","doc":"Four quarks with no antiquark are likewise excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.diquark_not_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.diquark_not_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L155-L157","doc":"**Confinement of the diquark.**  A two-quark object contains no colour\nsinglet, for grading reasons alone — at any `q`, with no dynamical input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.single_quark_not_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.single_quark_not_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L152-L153","doc":"A lone quark is not neutral — it cannot appear as a free state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.antibaryon_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.antibaryon_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L149-L150","doc":"An antibaryon `q̄q̄q̄` is neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.baryon_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.baryon_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L145-L147","doc":"A baryon `qqq` is neutral.  The singlet is the totally antisymmetric `ε`\ntensor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.meson_neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.meson_neutral","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L142-L143","doc":"A meson `q q̄` is neutral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_add","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L134-L138","doc":"Neutral states compose to neutral states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality_add","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L128-L132","doc":"Triality is additive under composition of objects — it is a grading, not\nmerely a label. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_iff_mod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.neutral_iff_mod","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L122-L126","doc":"Neutrality is a congruence: equal counts modulo three. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.instDecidableNeutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.instDecidableNeutral","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L117-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.Neutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.Neutral","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L110-L115","doc":"**Colour-neutral**: the object contains an `SU(3)` singlet.\n\nThis equivalence *is* the model — standard `SU(3)` representation theory, cited\nnot derived, since Mathlib has no `SU(3)` type.  Everything below is derived\nfrom it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.TrialitySelectionRule.triality","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/TrialitySelectionRule.lean#L106-L108","doc":"Triality of an object assembled from `a` fundamentals and `b`\nantifundamentals: the image of `a − b` in the centre `ℤ/3` of `SU(3)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}